# Backend

## Stack
Python 3.12, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy 2, Alembic, Pydantic 2, PostgreSQL (psycopg). Local infra: Docker Compose.

## Layout
- `app/api/` — REST routes only
- `app/core/` — config, security
- `app/db/` — database session, labeled demo fixtures (not invented market rates)
- `app/math_engine/` — pure Python math (no I/O, no LLM)
- `app/models/` — SQLAlchemy ORM
- `app/schemas/` — Pydantic DTOs (write these first)
- `app/services/` — business logic, OCR/LLM adapters, entitlements

## Database and auth
SQLAlchemy 2 style. Sessions from `app/db`. Schema in MVP via additive `create_all` (Alembic not initialized). Auth: email + password (PBKDF2), opaque session tokens in DB, Bearer header. No OAuth, email verification, or real payment processors.

## Uploads
Max 10 MB → HTTP 413. MIME: PDF, PNG, JPEG, WebP, DOCX → else HTTP 415.

## AI extractor
OCR/LLM extracts bill fields into Pydantic DTOs for user confirmation. Strip ```json fences. On any exception return `needs_manual_entry` — never fabricate bill values.

## Honest data
Tariffs, emission factors, benchmarks and savings coefficients are versioned config records with source, validity and status. Missing or unapproved config → `unavailable`, not a substitute number. No hardcoded KREM rates, Damu eligibility, or grid factor 0.892.

## Math engine
Implement in `backend/app/math_engine/` with pure Python. Do not change formulas. See SPECIFICATION.md §4: costs/effective rate, baseline, validation/anomalies, CO₂e (approved factor only), scenarios, constraints, enumerative optimizer, confidence, snapshots.
